{"agent_id":"J4Fq","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T19:48:02.406310708Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"df859f97-f277-40f6-8e03-da6942ccb78d","comment_uuid":"bf288f6c-f7fc-4ff9-9035-816b17d3cb54","author":"J4Fq","content":"Issue #67 reports that bootstrapping a fresh one-commit repository with daemon ensure --wait-ready spawns about 615 git subprocesses, mostly one 'git cat-file -t' per object from reconcile::publication::validate_source_objects, which takes 16-27 s on macOS and exceeds the 15 s daemon_readiness cap. The proposed durable fix is to batch object validation into a single 'git cat-file --batch-check' per pass. It also proposes memoizing validated OIDs across pin_source calls, which should likewise shorten the roughly five-minute first reconciliation on large hubs.","created_at":"2026-10-06T19:48:02.396619769Z","kind":"result"}}
